<p><a href="https://archive.org/details/timesgreatletter0000unse/page/246/mode/2up">Letter to the London <em>Times</em></a>, May 15, 1967:</p>
<blockquote><p>
Sir, is it not time that the Governments of great nations ceased to brag about their astronauts orbiting the earth? I have myself circled round the sun eighty times, without any publicity; a far greater achievement. I am in fact, just starting on my eighty-first orbit. And although I am an old man (I was born on May 10, 1887) I have been circling regularly from the day of my birth, if not before; and have suffered no ill effects.</p>
<p>Everyone does it.</p>
<p>Yours faithfully,</p>
<p>Frank Townshend
</p></blockquote>
